      "title": "Fiji declares national HIV emergency as Pacific nation grapples with surge in cases",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/sep/17/fiji-declares-national-hiv-emergency-infections-surge-health",
      "description": "<p>Government estimates that one in 60 adults in Fiji now living with HIV, as escalating use of methamphetamine fuels ‘epidemic’</p><p>Fiji has declared a national HIV emergency amid a spike in infections as the Pacific nation grapples with a correlating rise in methamphetamine use.</p><p>The country’s health and medical services minister, Dr Ratu Atonio Lalabalavu, said <a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/watch/?v=1386991873016868\">in a statement</a> on social media that an outbreak-level response was no longer sufficient to address what he described an “epidemic”.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/sep/17/fiji-declares-national-hiv-emergency-infections-surge-health\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-09-17T01:43:49"
